WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.089
Madhu, why do you care about quality?

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:07.570
I care about quality because without

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:13.550
ensuring quality care to all patients
that is patient-centric and offered in both

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.500
public and private sectors I just do not
see the TB burden coming down nor do I

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.500
see TB teaching the MTB strategy goals
of TB elimination.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.320
So from what I hear

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.489
fundamentally quality is at the heart of
how we are going to eliminate TB. Is that fair?

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:34.640
That's a fair comment. I still

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.140
think that even if you offered quality
care I think the world needs to address

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.070
the social determinants better I think
that is something we cannot really get

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:47.750
out of, but quality improvement something
we can do right away so and every

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.760
program, public or private, can institute
quality improvement without waiting for

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.800
anything else and while we are improving
quality of care and saving lives, public

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.820
systems need to address the underlying
social determinants. Mahdu, thank

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.020
you so much for doing this. This was
fantastic.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.579
Thank you, it's a pleasure.

